        "name": "pc-check-weighted-entries",
        "description": "Pure-logic validator that inspects a raw candidate list of weighted entries and returns an explicit validity result without exceptions. The outer input contract admits the raw candidate shape (a list, or a missing/null value) while the inner validation enforces the requested rules. Missing and null are distinct invalid outcomes; the result never raises and never coerces a malformed value into validity. This is a target typed-input interface; the runtime supplies step-local values through the inputs mapping and the kernel enforces global Tool policy before any real dispatch.",
        "content": "def check_weighted_entries(candidate):
    if not isinstance(candidate, list):
        return {"ok": False, "entries": []}
    if len(candidate) > 3:
        return {"ok": False, "entries": []}
    valid = True
    entries = []
    for item in candidate:
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            valid = False
            break
        if set(item.keys()) != {"label", "weight"}:
            valid = False
            break
        label = item.get("label")
        weight = item.get("weight")
        if not isinstance(label, str) or not isinstance(label, (int,)) or isinstance(label, bool) or not (1 <= len(label) <= 8):
            valid = False
            break
        if not isinstance(weight, int) or isinstance(weight, bool) or not (0 <= weight <= 1):
            valid = False
            break
        entries.append(item)
    result = {"ok": valid, "entries": entries if valid else []}
    return result"
